<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Deriving the ratio theorem</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>P divides AB internally in the ratio \({@m@} : {@n@}\), and \(\overrightarrow{OA} = \mathbf{a}\) and \(\overrightarrow{OB} = \mathbf{b}\). Complete the working.</p><div>(a) \(\overrightarrow{AP} =\) [[input:ans1]] \(\overrightarrow{AB}\) (a fraction) [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) \(\overrightarrow{AB} =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>(c) \(\overrightarrow{OP} = \overrightarrow{OA} + \overrightarrow{AP} = \mathbf{a} + \dfrac{ {@m@} }{ {@m+n@} }(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}) =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) The ratio \({@m@} : {@n@}\) splits AB into \({@m+n@}\) equal parts and AP is \({@m@}\) of them, so \(\overrightarrow{AP} = \dfrac{ {@m@} }{ {@m+n@} }\,\overrightarrow{AB}\).</p><p>(b) End minus start: \(\overrightarrow{AB} = \mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}\).</p><p>(c) \(\mathbf{a} + \dfrac{ {@m@} }{ {@m+n@} }(\mathbf{b} - \mathbf{a}) = \left(1 - \dfrac{ {@m@} }{ {@m+n@} }\right)\mathbf{a} + \dfrac{ {@m@} }{ {@m+n@} }\mathbf{b} = {@ta3@}\). This is the ratio theorem: \(\overrightarrow{OP} = \dfrac{n\mathbf{a} + m\mathbf{b}}{m + n}\). The weight on \(\mathbf{a}\) is the part of the ratio nearer B.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
